IRexp — licensing and attribution
=================================

IRexp redistributes extracted experimental fields only: IR band lists,
short NMR report strings, identifiers, and structures where present.
Article full text, PDFs, and figures are not redistributed.

Files
-----
  data/irexp_commercial.jsonl.gz       190,049 records
      Dataset of record (CC-BY-4.0 packaging, with per-record source licences).
      164,016 CC-BY/CC0 records, and 26,033 records from no-derivatives-
      licensed articles (26,028 CC-BY-NC-ND and 5 CC-BY-ND), marked
      nd_source_licence=true. The source licence on each record is kept.
  data/irexp_non_commercial.jsonl.gz    39,000 records
      CC-BY-NC (38,277) and CC-BY-NC-SA (723). Source licences are kept.
      The 723 CC-BY-NC-SA records carry both NonCommercial and ShareAlike
      conditions and must not be relicensed as CC-BY.
  data/irexp_sharealike.jsonl.gz         1,897 records
      CC-BY-SA (9) and Chemotion CC-BY-SA-4.0 (1,888). Remix only under
      CC-BY-SA-4.0; do not relicense as CC-BY.
  data/structure_quarantine.jsonl.gz     8,457 ids
      8,158 withheld tier-X ids and 299 formula–NMR flagged ids.
  data/seen_papers.txt.gz
      PMC identifiers scanned during harvest.
  data/SHA256SUMS.txt
      SHA256 checksums of the files above.

Headline total: 230,946 records. Not deposited: 8,789 harvested records
without an established licence.

Licences
--------
The CC-BY file is the dataset of record. Filter on nd_source_licence to
keep only records whose source licence permits adaptation. The
non-commercial and ShareAlike files keep their source licences. Every
record carries license, license_raw, license_source, and license_pool.

Attribution
-----------
Cite the IRexp Data Descriptor and this deposit. Attribute each record
through source_doi or pmcid.

